<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agilulf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 616</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agilulf was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from 590 to 616. Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, he became king by marrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodelinda">Theodelinda</a>, widow of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/authari">Authari</a>, and consolidated Lombard rule, fighting the Byzantine exarchate of Ravenna and making peace with Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i">Gregory the Great</a>. Under Theodelinda's influence he allowed their son Adaloald to be baptised a Catholic, a step towards the conversion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agilulf.jpg" alt="Agilulf" width="245" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel Wolgemut, Wilhelm Pleydenwurff (Text: Hartmann Schedel) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuremberg_chronicles_f_150r_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
